I just saw:

> The fiery blade burns the paper golem. You kill the paper golem.
> X - an unlabeled scroll. Y - 2 unlabeled scrolls.

[using 3.4.3 - vanilla, unpatched, MS-Windows.]

I don't think so. If a paper golem dies to Fire
Brand's special attack, there is no way it should
then be able to drop unlabeled scrolls. It shouldn't
be "killed", surely it should be "consumed" or
"destroyed".

Arguably the PC should take some heat damage, too.

IMO

xanthian, altar squatting a wizard on level 2, with
my good friends Juiblex and Yeenoghu and a dozen or
so peaceful goblins and orcs. My Wizard "Orc Kibble"
just got his first succubus Succulent Susie (and
first hot date) via orc-sacrifice. This goes much
slower without a ring of slow digestion or a scroll
of scare monster, but a wand of lightning let me put
Elbereths on three sides of the altar, and Orc
Kibble is making do, so far with Fire Brand, Magic
Bane, and DragonBane as sacrifice gifts. The kid
hasn't quite got the trick of the timing to start
getting spellbooks instead of artifacts, though.
Magic Bane is already at expert, which is why he's
trying to get Fire Brand up to basic. This is sort
of the inverse of the protection racket: Susie got
all the gold, and Orc Kibble is already XL 9 and
adding XPs like mad. I suspect skipping Mines
entirely might be a good strategy, especially if
some kind newt death-drops a luckstone in the next
